    where the line sits: which tools have the contractual terms that make business use
    defensible, which consumer tiers train on what you paste into them, what has to be
    de-identified first, and what should never leave your systems at all.</p>
    <p>Practices come out of it with a written AI usage policy their team actually
    follows, not a prohibition everyone quietly ignores — which is the real risk,
