faq:
  - q: "Will this work for staff who aren't technical?"
    a: "That's who it's built for. No coding, no setup, no prompt-engineering theory. If someone can write an email to a client, they can do this — the program starts from that assumption rather than treating it as a limitation."
  - q: "Can AI do the actual accounting?"
    a: "No, and we'd be worried about anyone selling you that. It drafts, summarises, restructures and explains. The judgement, the review and the sign-off stay with the accountant — which is also what your professional obligations require. The saving is in the writing and reading around the work, and that is most of the week."
  - q: "We're a five-person practice. Is this only for big firms?"
    a: "Small practices tend to get more out of it, because there's nobody to delegate the drafting to. The program is priced and paced for SME teams — it's the same three months whether you send two people or twenty."
  - q: "What about the July to October crunch?"
    a: "Start before it, not during. Teams that come through in autumn go into tax season with the follow-up and drafting workflows already built. Starting mid-crunch is the one timing we'd steer you away from."
  - q: "Do we need to buy new software?"
    a: "Not to start. Most practices already have a paid ChatGPT, Copilot or Claude seat somewhere in the business, and the training is tool-agnostic in any case. Where a tool is genuinely needed we'll say so and say why."
